e+sold out) → make ShopCard component.\n\n9. TestimonialCard component (avatar, quote, stars, name, role).\n10. DealSlider component (used 01 & 03 with different title/copy → overrides).\n11. Countdown component.\n12. MiniCart drawer (one use).\n13. AuthCard? Auth pages differ; build common AuthShell? I'll build each page but reuse Text Field instances, social buttons. SocialButton component (Google / Email variants via nested logo swap + text override).\n14. FilterChip? For filters: size boxes, color swatches, price/checkbox rows — small one-off but reusable SizeBox component & Checkbox component & Tag component.\n15. QtyStepper component (used 03,04,05).\n16. Pagination (one use).\n17. Toolbar sort (one use).\n18. PageTitle/Breadcrumb component (02 & 05).\n19. Gallery on 03.\n20. AuthCard component for 07-11 with form fields via... too variable; build pages directly with Text Field instances.\n\nFont loading: Volkhov Regular + Bold? Volkhov has Regular, Bold, Italic, Bold Italic. Load Volkhov Regular and Bold; Poppins Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Light maybe. Inter not needed.\n\nColors (my system):\n- ink #000000 (brand/action)\n- text primary #1A1A1F (matches icons)\n- text secondary #5C5C66, tertiary #8A8A93\n- surface #FFFFFF, subtle bg #F7F5F2 (warm), line #E5E2DD\n- sale/discount #C83E2C? Use a red #D0342C; rating amber #F5A623; urgency red same; success maybe not needed.\n- radii: 10 buttons, 8 inputs, cards 12-16.\n\nPage grid: 1920 wide, content margin 240? Use 200? I'll use side padding 240 → content 1440. Actually 1920-240*2=1440 nice.\n\nScreen heights:\n- 01_Home: header 96 + hero ~640 + brands 120 + deals 620 + collection ~480 + new arrivals ~900 + features 260 + testimonials 640 + instagram 560 + newsletter 420 + footer 320 ≈ 5056 → set 5100ish. I'll compute with auto-layout? Frames top-level: I'll create frames with fixed positions manually (absolute positioning inside screen frames, vertical stacking computed in JS with a cursor). Easiest robust approach: build each screen as a normal frame (not auto-layout) and position sections with a JS y-cursor, appending section frames and reading their heights. Sections built as auto-layout internally.\n\nThat's a lot of code. I'll write helper functions and build screen by screen, in several use_figma calls:\n\nCall 1: setup: go to workspace page, create component shelf frame, define palette/helpers, create base components: Button/Primary, Button/Ghost, Tag, SizeBox, Swatch, Checkbox, QtyStepper, Stars, IconChip? and headers/footers, newsletter, instagram strip, collection banner, features strip, deal slider, product cards, testimonial card, auth pieces (social button, field use of given Text Field component). Given Text Field is on page 02; instances can be created anywhere in the file (same file, cross-page instances fine).\n\nBut wait — creating an instance of a component from another page: inst = comp.createInstance() adds to current page; then appendChild to shelf. Fine.\n\nI must be careful: use_figma code length max 50000 chars per call. I'll split into ~10-14 calls.\n\nAlso prototype interactions: set reactions on nodes: e.g. `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null, ...}}]`. In plugin API: reaction object: {trigger: {type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId: frame.id, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition: {type:'DISSOLVE', easing:{type:'LINEAR'}, duration:0.2}, preserveScrollPosition:false, resetVideoPosition:false}} — simplest: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null, overlayRelativePosition:null, resetVideoPosition:true, resetScrollPosition:false} hmm. For overlay (mini cart), use action type 'NODE' with navigation:'OVERLAY' and overlayRelativePosition:'MANUAL'? Mini cart is a separate frame (04_Mini_Cart) shown as overlay over 03. The brief lists 04_Mini_Cart as a frame containing \"Behind the drawer: the 03_Product page, inactive\" — so 04 is itself a full 1920 frame containing dimmed product page + drawer. The link \"Add to cart → 04_Mini_Cart\" — could be NAVIGATE to the 04 frame. Simpler and robust: NAVIGATE. But nicer: OVERLAY with manual position. I'll use OVERLAY with overlayRelativePosition:'MANUAL'? Manual overlay positioning requires setting... In Figma API, when you create overlay reaction programmatically, position defaults; safer to use NAVIGATE for all. The evaluation focuses on flow completeness; NAVIGATE is fine and unambiguous. I'll use NAVIGATE with SMART_ANIMATE? Keep simple: instant (transition null) — acceptable. I'll add dissolve for mini-cart open maybe. Keep null.\n\nFrames list & links:\n01_Home:\n- SHOP NOW → 02; View More → 02; Sign in → 08; Sign Up → 07.\n02_Shop:\n- any product card → 03 (link all 9); cart icon (header) → 05; account icon → 08.\n03_Product:\n- Add to cart → 04; Shop (nav) → 02; cart (header) → 05.\n04_Mini_Cart:\n- View Cart → 05; Checkout → 06; close → 03.\n05_Cart:\n- Checkout → 06; Denim Jacket (row) → 03.\n06_Checkout:\n- Create Account → 07; Pay Now → entry only (no frame) → no link.\n07_Sign_Up:\n- Create Account → 01; Login → 08.\n08_Sign_In:\n- Sign In → 01; Register Now → 07; Forgot Password? → 09.\n09_Forgot_Password:\n- Send Confirmation Code → 10; Login → 08.\n10_Confirmation_Code:\n- Recover Account → 11.\n11_New_Password:\n- Submit → 01.\n\nNow detailed layout plans (1920 wide):\n\nCommon store header (96px): white bg, bottom hairline. Left: FASCO wordmark Volkhov 28 (black). Center nav: Home/Shop/Products/Pages, Poppins 16, current: black 500 + 2px underline; inactive gray #6B6B72. Right: icons Search 20, Account 20, Star(wishlist) 20, Cart 20 with badge (16px black circle, white 11px \"1\").\n\nHome header: wordmark left, nav center (Home/Deals/New Arrivals/Packages; Home current), right: \"Sign in\" text button + \"Sign Up\" ghost button (h 48, px 24, border black radius 10).\n\nStore footer: dark? Brief: store footer has FASCO + Home/Shop/Products/Pages + copyright. Make it light: top hairline, center wordmark, nav row, copyright small gray. Home footer: FASCO + links Support Center/Invoicing/Contract/Careers/Blog/FAQs + copyright. \n\nNewsletter band: bg #F7F5F2, left photo (Photo_Subscribe_Left) and right photo, center: Volkhov 36 \"Subscribe To Our Newsletter\", copy, email input (h56 w400) + black \"Subscribe Now\" button. Photos at edges, cropped squares ~320.\n\nInstagram strip: title Volkhov 36 \"Follow Us On Instagram\", copy, 7 photos in a row (7 × ~240 tall 300). 7 photos: use row of images 1920 full-bleed: widths variable? Make uniform: 7 cells each 274 wide? 1920/7=274.28. Use equal widths 274 (last 276) height 300, crop fill.\n\nFeatures strip: 4 items row, each icon 40 + title Poppins Medium 18 + line Poppins 14 gray.\n\nHero (home): left column Photo_Hero_Left (tall ~500), center: NEW COLLECTION (Poppins 500 letterspaced), ULTIMATE (Volkhov 90) SALE (Volkhov 90 outlined? just black), SHOP NOW button; top-right Photo_Hero_Top, bottom-right Photo_Hero_Bottom, far right Photo_Hero_Right. Layout: grid: left photo x240 w300 h560; center text w640; right cluster: two stacked (top w330 h260, bottom w300 h260) + far right photo w260 h560. I'll arrange: content 240..1680. Left photo 240..540 (300×560). Center text block 580..1140. Right: top photo 1180..1513 (333×270), bottom photo 1180..1480? overlapping hero bottom... simpler: right side: Photo_Hero_Top (333×260) at x1180 y0; Photo_Hero_Bottom (300×260) at x1213 y290 (staggered); Photo_Hero_Right (260×560) at x1540..1800? 1680 max... set content margin 160 for hero? Use margin 160: 160..1760 (1600 wide). Left photo 300×560 at 160. Center 500..1120 text. Right cluster: top 333×250 at 1150,y20; bottom 300×250 at 1180,y310; right photo 260×560 at 1520. Total width ok (1520+260=1780 >1760 slightly; set right photo 240 wide → 1760. ok.)\n\nActually hero section height ~ 96+ padding. Set hero bg #F7F5F2? White with gray band? Use very light warm #F