19, Megen 6:68, Suzan 6:18\nLogos: Gmail 6:69, Google 6:23\nIcons: Account 6:15, Cart 6:16, Chevron_Down 6:17, Chevron_Left 6:20, Chevron_Right 6:21, Close 6:22, Compare 6:24, Delivery 6:25, Eye 6:26, Guarantee 6:28, Lock 6:29, Question 6:30, Returns 6:31, Search 6:33, Share 6:34, Shipping 6:35, Star 6:37, Support 6:38, Trophy 6:40, View_Grid 6:41, View_List 6:42\nGiven: Button 1:24, Text Field 1:27.\n\nNow write helper library reused across calls. Since each use_figma call is independent JS execution, I need to redefine helpers each call. I'll craft a compact helper preamble (~120 lines) and paste per call.\n\nHelpers:\n```\nconst PAGE=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('8:2'));\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(PAGE);\nconst fonts=[['Volkhov','Regular'],['Volkhov','Bold'],['Poppins','Regular'],['Poppins','Medium'],['Poppins','Semi Bold'],['Poppins','Light']];\nfor(const [family,style] of fonts) await figma.loadFontAsync({family,style});\nconst C={ink:{r:0,g:0,b:0},txt:{r:0.102,g:0.102,b:0.122},sub:{r:0.42,g:0.42,b:0.46},mut:{r:0.62,g:0.61,b:0.63},line:{r:0.9,g:0.89,b:0.87},bg:{r:0.973,g:0.965,b:0.953},white:{r:1,g:1,b:1},red:{r:0.75,g:0.22,b:0.17},amber:{r:0.96,g:0.65,b:0.14},lilac:{r:0.78,g:0.72,b:0.87},blue:{r:0.35,g:0.45,b:0.65}};\nfunction T(s,style={},...){...}\n```\n\nText helper:\n```\nfunction txt(chars,{f='Poppins',s='Regular',z=14,c=C.txt,ls,la,align}={}){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:f,style:s};t.fontSize=z;t.characters=chars;t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:c}];if(align)t.textAlignHorizontal=align;return t;}\n```\nFrame helper:\n```\nfunction fr(name,{w,h,fill,stroke,r,pad=[0,0,0,0],gap=0,dir='NONE',align,counter}={}){...}\n```\nMaybe simpler: build with explicit code per section; helpers for text/button/icon/photo:\n\n```\nasync function comp(id){return await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);}\nfunction instOf(c){return c.createInstance();}\nasync function photo(id,w,h,r=0){const i=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)).createInstance();i.resize(w,h);if(r)i.cornerRadius=r;return i;}\nasync function icon(id,size,color){const i=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)).createInstance();i.resize(size,size);setPaint(i,color);return i;}\nfunction setPaint(node,color){if(node.fills!==undefined&&Array.isArray(node.fills)){try{node.fills=node.fills.map(f=>f.type==='SOLID'?{type:'SOLID',color}:f);}catch(e){}} if(node.strokes!==undefined){try{node.strokes=node.strokes.map(f=>f.type==='SOLID'?{type:'SOLID',color}:f);}catch(e){}} if(node.children)node.children.forEach(ch=>setPaint(ch,color));}\n```\nCareful: photo instances have fills IMAGE — mapping only SOLID leaves image intact. Setting strokes on instance root may throw if none — try/catch.\n\nResize icons: icons have varied aspect (20×20, 24×24, 15×15, 60×60, 18×18, 20×16). Resize keeping aspect: helper icon(id,w) scale by width: `const r=w/i.width; i.rescale? ` — instances have rescale? There's `i.resize(w,h)`. Compute h=i.height*w/i.width.\n\nAuto layout: I'll mostly use absolute positioning with computed coordinates to reduce fragility. But that's a lot of manual math across ~11 screens. Middle ground: use auto-layout for rows/columns within sections (headers, footers, cards) and absolute y-stacking for sections: after building a section frame (auto-layout with known width 1920), append to page frame? If page frame is not auto-layout, appending sets position 0,0; then set x=0,y=cursor; cursor+=section.height. Section heights known after layout. \n\nI'll make screen frames plain frames with clipsContent true; sections appended and y-set manually.\n\nAlright, component shelf: I'll create components on workspace page directly (components can live on the page; they're not \"frames\" that interfere with the 11 named frames as long as named clearly, e.g. inside a Section \"Components\" or just a FRAME \"Components · Local\" containing COMPONENT nodes). Top-level requirement \"Build exactly the 11 frames\" — extra top-level frames might be flagged? To be safe, put local components inside one FRAME named \"FASCO Design System · Local Components\" — that's an extra top-level frame though. Alternative: put components on the same page but as top-level COMPONENT nodes (not frames). Top-level components are allowed; \"11 frames\" refers to the screens. I'll place components as top-level nodes at x=-3000 area. Hmm — component nodes at top level are fine.\n\nActually cleaner: create a separate page \"Local Components\"? That adds a page — allowed? \"Keep existing unrelated content intact. Do not replace reference pages\" — adding a page is fine but the brief says deliver 11 frames; extra page could be noise. I'll keep components as top-level COMPONENT nodes on the workspace page, arranged neatly in a labeled group area at negative x. Wait, can components be children of the page directly? Yes.\n\nHmm, but nice organization: I'll create a SECTION? Sections on page top-level also fine. Keep simple: components directly on page at x -3200.. with a label text \"Local components\" — text node top-level also fine.\n\nNow the plan for each use_figma call:\n\nCall A: setup page, fonts, create core small components:\n- Btn/Black (auto h 56 pad 32/16? given: h56 r10 black, Poppins 16 white. I'll do padding 0 horizontal with fixed? Use auto-layout: horizontal, center, padding L/R 28, height fixed 56, radius 10)\n- Btn/Ghost (white, border ink 1, ink text)\n- UI/Tag (chip: border line, radius 20, Poppins 13, pad 8/14)\n- UI/SizeBox (44×44 border line, Poppins 14; selected variant via instance override? I'll create two components: SizeBox and SizeBox/Selected? Component reuse with states: create COMPONENT_SET? Variants add complexity; simpler two components named \"SizeBox/Default\",\"SizeBox/Selected\" — naming with slash groups them. OK.\n- UI/Swatch (28×28 circle; color set per instance override fill; selected gets outer ring — I'll implement swatch as 32×32 frame with ring border hidden? visibility override on ring). Simpler: Swatch/Default (plain circle) & Swatch/Selected (ring + circle). Two comps.\n- UI/Checkbox/Unchecked & Checked? Only unchecked needed. One comp: box 18 border + label? Label varies → checkbox box only; label separate text.\n- UI/Stepper (− 01 +) component w auto layout.\n- UI/Stars5 (row of 5 star icons amber) component.\n- UI/CountdownBox (number+label) and CountdownRow (4 boxes + colons?) For deals: 02 Days 06 Hr 05 Mins 30 Sec → 4 boxes. Component Countdown with 4 boxes.\n- Card/ProductArrival (photo placeholder + brand + stars + reviews + name + price + almost sold out)\n- Card/ProductShop (photo + soldout badge slot + name + price row)\n- Card/Testimonial (avatar+stars+quote+name+role)\n- Nav stuff: Header/Home, Header/Store (with underlines + badge as hidable), Footer/Home, Footer/Store\n- Section/Newsletter, Section/Instagram, Section/Collection, Section/Features, Section/DealSlider\n- Auth: Btn/Social (logo+label), Auth/Field? just use given Text Field instances.\n- Cart/QtyStepper same as UI/Stepper.\n- PageTitle/Breadcrumb component? small; make component PageHead with title + breadcrumb texts (override per page).\n\nThat's Call A (big). Then:\n\nCall B: build 01_Home using components + hero + brands.\nCall C: build 02_Shop.\nCall D: build 03_Product.\nCall E: build 04_Mini_Cart (clone 03, overlay, drawer, badge).\nCall F: build 05_Cart.\nCall G: build 06_Checkout.\nCall H: build 07,08 sign up/in.\nCall I: build 09,10,11.\nCall J: prototype reactions.\nCalls K+: screenshots + fixes.\n\nInstance text overrides helper:\n```\nfunction setText(inst,name,chars){const n=inst.findOne(x=>x.name===name&&x.type==='TEXT');if(n){n.characters=chars;}return n;}\n```\nfindOne on instance works.\n\nSwap photo inside card instance:\n```\nconst ph=inst.findOne(x=>x.name==='Photo'); ph.swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(pid));\n```\nNested instance children: findOne returns nested instance; swapComponent allowed on instances. \n\nVisibility override: `n.visible=false` on instance child — allowed.\n\nReactions API: node.reactions=[{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'},action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:target.id,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'DISSOLVE',easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'},duration:0.2},resetVideoPosition:false,resetScrollPosition:false}}]? The exact action shape: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition, preserveScrollPosition}. Let me use minimal: action={type:'NODE',destinationId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:null,preserveScrollPosition:false}. I recall Reaction action requires: type 'NODE'|'URL'|'BACK'|'CLOSE'; navigation 'NAVIGATE'|'OVERLAY'|'CHANGE_TO'; destinationId; transition; preserveScrollPosition; overlayRelativePosition; resetVideoPosition; resetScrollPosition. Providing subset might throw. I'll test on two nodes first and inspect error.\n\nLet me also handle: top-level frames must be named exactly: \"01_Home\", \"02_Shop\", \"03_Product\", \"04_Mini_Cart\", \"05_Cart\", \"06_Checkout\", \"07_Sign_Up\", \"08_Sign_In\", \"09_Forgot_Password\", \"10_Confirmation_Code\", \"11_New_Password\". Place them in grid: x positions spaced: screens at x=0, y staggered; each screen 1920 wide. Arrange in rows of 2: \n01 (0,0) h~5400; 02 at x=2160,y=0 h~4600; 03 x=0? Better: single column with 240 gaps is simplest: x=0, y cumulative. Widths all 1920. Heights: 01 ~5600, 02 ~5200, 03 ~5600, 04 ~5600 (matches 03 since clone), 05 ~2400, 06 ~3000, 07-11 1080 each. Total ~ 5600+5200+5600+5600+2400+3000+5*1080+gaps(10*240=2400) ≈ 35k. Fine.\n\nMini cart clone: 04 height = 03 height exactly.\n\nNow typography scale:\n- Display (hero ULTIMATE/SALE): Volkhov Bold 110\n- H1 page titles: Volkhov Bold 40? Volkhov has Bold? Volkhov family styles: Regular, Italic, Bold, Bold Italic. Yes.\n- Section titles: Volkhov Bold 36? original kit uses Volkhov regular. Use Volkhov Regular for headings (elegant serif), Bold for emphasis numbers. I'll use Volkhov Regular 36 section titles, 28-40.\n- Wordmark FASCO: Volkhov Regular 30, letterspacing? fine.\n- Body: Poppin