(w 440 h 340, white r16 shadow subtle, padding 32): quote icon? Just: avatar 56 + name/role? Kit: quote text first, stars, divider, avatar+name+role. I'll do: stars row top, quote (Poppins 14, 4 lines), bottom row avatar 48 + name 15 Medium + role 12 sub. Middle card (James K.) scale emphasis: white with border ink? Make active card slightly elevated: shadow bigger + border 1 ink. prev/next arrows: circles at sides or below with dots? Brief requires prev/next chevron buttons — place two circular buttons bottom center-right. Current: James K. → James card is middle/active. \n\nInstagram: white; title + copy centered; row of 7 images full-bleed h 300: widths: [147,143,220,147,330,330,330] original aspect; I'll crop all to uniform: w=1920/7≈274.28 → use 275×6=1650 +270; simpler all 274 except last 276. Fine: w274 h300 r0.\n\nNewsletter: bg #F7F5F2? Testimonials already that; alternate: newsletter bg white with photos at sides. Layout: full width band h 420: left photo 360×420 (cropped), right photo 360×420, center content: title Volkhov 36, copy 14 sub w560 centered, row: input (w 400 h 56 white border r10, placeholder \"michael@example.com\") + button black \"Subscribe Now\". \n\nFooters:\nHome footer: 1920×300, border top: center column: FASCO Volkhov 28; links row: Support Center · Invoicing · Contract · Careers · Blog · FAQs (Poppins 14 sub); copyright 13 muted. \nStore footer: same but links Home · Shop · Products · Pages.\n\nHome total height: 88+760+150+720+? Collection banner on home too! Order per kit: Hero, Brands, Deals, New Arrivals? Actually original FASCO: hero, brands, deals, collection(\"Men Collection\" banner is actually on shop/product pages...). Brief says 01 must include Collection banner too. Order (my decision): Hero → Brands → Deals → Collection banner → New Arrivals → Features → Testimonials → Instagram → Newsletter → Footer. \n\nCollection banner: h 560 bg #EFEAE4 full width: photo left 460×460 at x240 y50 r16? Kit style: photo square left, content right. Content: \"Men Collection\" Volkhov 36 + \"Classic Gentleman\" Poppins 14 sub ls?; chips row 4 (Flat Cap, Cotton Shirt, Suspender, Leather Shoes); \"DESCRIPTION\" 12 Medium ls1 gray; copy 14 sub w 560; row: \"Size: M\" (14) ; \"$100.00\" Volkhov 24; Buy Now button.\n\n01 height ≈ 88+760+150+720+560+1950+220+? testimonials ~700 + instagram ~520 + newsletter 420 + footer 300 = let me sum: 88+760=848; +150=998; +720=1718; +560=2278; +1950=4228; +220=4448; +700=5148; +520=5668; +420=6088; +300=6388. → 6400.\n\n02_Shop: header 88; page head (title+breadcrumb) ~160 bg #F7F5F2?; toolbar 64; main: sidebar + grid: product card shop: photo 458×540 r16 + name + price → ~640; 3 rows = 3*640+2*40=2000; pagination 80; then collection 560; features 220; instagram 520; newsletter 420; footer 300. Total ≈ 88+160+64+ (pad 40 + 2000 + 40) + 80 +560+220+520+420+300 ≈ 4492 → 4500.\n\n03_Product: header 88; product section: gallery+info ~ 900; actions row inside info; delivery box inside info; then People Also Loved 720; collection 560; features 220; newsletter 420; footer 300. Total ≈ 88+900+720+560+220+420+300=3208 → 3250. 04 same 3250.\n\n05_Cart: header 88; page head 160; table ~ 360; total box ~ 300; newsletter 420; footer 300 → ~1700. Make 1750.\n\n06_Checkout: header 88; title 120; form columns ~ 1300; newsletter 420; footer 300 → ~2300.\n\nAuth pages 1920×1080 each.\n\nOK. Time to write Call A. Keep code robust: define helpers, create components in a tidy row area at x=-3600 (outside screens). Components as COMPONENT nodes via figma.createComponent().\n\nImportant: component children — for auto-layout components, set after creating. I'll write a `mk` helper for frames with autolayout config:\n\n```\nfunction AL(node,{dir='HORIZONTAL',gap=0,pad=[0,0,0,0],align='CENTER',counter='CENTER',w,h}={}){\n node.layoutMode=dir;node.itemSpacing=gap;\n node.paddingLeft=pad[0];node.paddingTop=pad[1];node.paddingRight=pad[2];node.paddingBottom=pad[3];\n node.primaryAxisAlignItems=align;node.counterAxisAlignItems=counter;\n if(w!==undefined){if(dir==='HORIZONTAL'){node.layoutMode... }\n```\nSizing: for auto-layout frames use primaryAxisSizingMode/counterAxisSizingMode 'AUTO' or fixed via resize. I'll handle inline.\n\nSimplify: I'll write helper `H(gap,pad)` returns config; and set fills/strokes/radius via `sty(node,{f,s,r,sw})`.\n\nLet me now carefully write Call A code. Also create paint styles? Not necessary.\n\nOne more consideration: setText override requires fonts loaded for that text's font — loaded.\n\nFor the given Text Field component (1:27): I'll create instances for form fields; override Label & Placeholder texts; width override: resize instance to needed width (auto-layout vertical; Input child should be stretch? The component's Input frame w420 fixed; resizing instance width to e.g. 640 — with layoutMode vertical, child Input layoutAlign? probably not stretch; I may need to set child's layoutAlign='STRETCH' via override — allowed? layoutAlign override on instance child: yes allowed. I'll set inst child Input.layoutAlign='STRETCH' and placeholder text. Actually simpler: build my own Field component? Brief: reuse given components — I should reuse Button and Text Field where sensible. I'll use Text Field instances in newsletter, checkout, auth forms. Widths: default 420 ok for many; newsletter input 400→ resize 400 (shrink). For checkout full-width 560/2-col 272: resize; fix child stretch. I'll write helper `field(label,placeholder,w)` that creates instance, sets texts, resizes w, sets Input child layoutAlign STRETCH, and the root layoutMode vertical — need root counterAxisSizing? The root is VERTICAL auto-layout width 420 fixed? Its w=420; resizing instance sets width. Child Input w 420 fixed inside → set layoutAlign stretch. Also Label fixed width 38? label has own width; fine (hug). Placeholder hug. OK.\n\nAnd given Button (1:24): 207×56 black r10 Poppins Regular 16. I'll use MY button components for most buttons (need ghost etc.