s/almost sold out texts aren't in must-include for shop; but fine to leave? \"Almost Sold Out\" on all would be wrong-ish. Better: for shop cards, set reviews text to '' (empty) and 'Almost Sold Out' to ''. For old price: set reviews text to old price struck through? Must include \"old price where given\". I'll set the reviews-line text to e.g. \"$14.00\" with strikethrough textDecoration and color t3, positioned right after price? Actually layout order: name row, reviews, price, almost sold out. Simplest: set reviews text to '' and put old price into 'Almost Sold Out' line? No — better: set 'Almost Sold Out' line to '' and reviews line to '' ; then for old price, append strikethrough to the price text: \" $11.00 $14.00\" with old struck? Can't have mixed styles easily without setRangeFont... Actually you can: t.characters='$11.00  $14.00'; t.setRangeStrikethrough(9,15,true); setRangeFills for t3. Fine.\n\nGrid: col children: toolbar + grid. Grid 3 cols wrap.\n\nThen pagination centered. Then Collection banner, Features, Instagram, Newsletter, Footer/Store.\n\nThen main height fix: main fixed 2700; grid 3 rows of ~460+32 → ~1500 + toolbar 48 + pagination 48 + gaps ~ 1700. main 2700 too tall; set main to AUTO height: primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO.\n\nLet me write next call: add grid + pagination to col, set main auto height, then stack remaining sections.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4989fa14-2e7d-4d0d-bbb8-4573dd6d6ae6","uuid":"8d32087d-01a4-41d3-b99b-06592e5551f4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:28:08.732Z","thinking_duration_ms":27035}
